11	 *   5. the effective patch is `{ einvoice_uuid }` with NO transition — a naked
12	 *      field edit in a frozen state, which the rule rejects
13	 *
14	 * This used to throw. The agent had proposed something legal; an unrelated
15	 * ownership hold made it illegal, and because the deferral is built AFTER the
16	 * transaction returns, the throw skipped it — so the work was denied under a
17	 * misattributed reason AND the approval card was lost.
18	 *
19	 * The fix is not to weaken validation but to stop splitting the write: when the
20	 * residual fails and fields were held, nothing commits and the ENTIRE proposal
21	 * defers as one approval unit. The control test proves the hold is what changes
22	 * the outcome — the identical agent write commits outright when no human owns
23	 * `status`.
